# ── Credentials and signing material ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Nothing matching these has ever been tracked here — checked before adding
# them, against every path in `git ls-files`. They are here because this
# repository is PUBLIC and its history is permanent: a key committed once is
# disclosed even if the next commit deletes it, and this account has published
# secrets to a public repo twice. The cost of the rule is nil; the cost of the
# omission is a rotation.
#
# Both lanes are covered on purpose — see LANES.md. The Windows agent owns
# `android/` and its keystore, and a Mac cannot test what that lane commits.

# Keys and certificates, any lane
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.der
*.cer

# Android signing (the Windows lane's)
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties

# Apple signing and App Store Connect
*.p8
AuthKey_*.p8
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
.appstoreconnect/

# Environment and service credentials. `.env.example` is deliberately kept:
# a committed template is how the next person knows which variables exist.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
service-account*.json
*-service-account.json

# Anything a developer names as a secret
secrets.dart
**/secrets/

